1/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-10-30T02:54:31.588263+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1pt.1","local_name":"sase-1pt.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1pt","agent_clan_generation":"20261029181311","bead_id":"sase-1pt.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1pt[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]End agent commit stages at a durable publication enqueue[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]A no-conflict sase agent commit stage (provider done to done.json) [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]drops from a median of about four minutes to about one, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-core pin-only rebase conflicts stop costing an LLM repair [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]turn, while every sidecar write the commit path owes today is still[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]made. The agent's own declared commits stay synchronous and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]host-verified. Prompt-archive, agent-hood, Referenced By, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]artifact-link publication is durably queued before the stage ends, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]then drained by a host-owned background publisher, with today's [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]inline drain as an automatic fallback.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]commit_stage_async_publication.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/commit_stage_async_publication.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1pt[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1pt/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop t